module

public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Radical.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier.AffineComplement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier.StalkwiseRegular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierWeilDivisor

/-!
# The reduced induced structure on the complement of a dense affine open is an effective Cartier
divisor

Let `X` be a Noetherian scheme with affine diagonal, let `U ⊆ X` be a dense affine open and
suppose the local ring of `X` at every point outside `U` is a unique factorization domain.  The
complement `X ∖ U` is then the support of an effective Cartier divisor, and this file proves the
sharper statement that the *reduced induced* closed subscheme on `X ∖ U` — the vanishing ideal
sheaf of that closed set — is itself an effective Cartier divisor.

## Main results

* `UniqueFactorizationMonoid.radical_span_singleton`: in a unique factorization monoid the
  radical of the ideal generated by a nonzero element `f` is generated by the radical of `f`,
  the product of the distinct prime factors of `f`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_vanishingIdeal_compl_denseAffineOpen`: the
  vanishing ideal sheaf of the complement of a dense affine open is an effective Cartier
  divisor.

## The argument

`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_compl_affineOpen` already produces *some*
effective Cartier divisor `I` whose support is `X ∖ U`; it is the product of the vanishing ideal
sheaves of the irreducible components of `X ∖ U`, so it is not reduced where two components
meet.  The vanishing ideal sheaf of `X ∖ U` is the radical of `I`, because the vanishing ideal
of the support of an ideal sheaf is its radical, so the whole question is local and purely
algebraic: *is the radical of an effective Cartier divisor again one?*

It is, when the local rings are factorial.  Around a point `x` of the complement, `I` is
generated on an affine open `V` by a nonzerodivisor `f`, so its stalk at `x` is generated by the
germ of `f`, which is nonzero because a nonzerodivisor survives localization.  Radicals commute
with localization, so the stalk of the radical of `I` at `x` is the radical of a nonzero
principal ideal of the factorial local ring `𝒪_{X, x}`.  In a unique factorization monoid that
radical is again principal, generated by the product of the distinct prime factors of the
generator, which is nonzero and hence a nonzerodivisor of the domain `𝒪_{X, x}`.  A closed
subscheme whose ideal is generated at every point of it by a nonzerodivisor of the local ring is
an effective Cartier divisor.

## Implementation notes

The algebraic heart is `UniqueFactorizationMonoid.exists_dvd_pow_iff_radical_dvd`: an element is
divided by some power of `f` exactly when it is divided by the radical of `f`.  Membership of
`b` in the radical of `(f)` is the left-hand side and membership in `(radical f)` is the right,
so the two ideals coincide, and the proof is just that translation.

The hypothesis of factoriality is `UniqueFactorizationMonoid` on the stalk, which is stated for
a commutative monoid with zero and so carries no domain structure of its own; the domain
structure is recovered the way
`AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_codimension_one_of_uniqueFactorizationMonoid`
recovers it, from cancellativity and nontriviality.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BCW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BCW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EGJ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EGJ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG8)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace UniqueFactorizationMonoid

/-- **The radical of a principal ideal in a unique factorization monoid is principal**, generated
by the radical of the generator — the product of its distinct prime factors.  An element lies in
the radical of `(f)` exactly when some power of it is divisible by `f`, which happens exactly
when it is divisible by the radical of `f`. -/
theorem radical_span_singleton {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [NormalizationMonoid R]
    [UniqueFactorizationMonoid R] {f : R} (hf : f ≠ 0) :
    (Ideal.span {f}).radical = Ideal.span {UniqueFactorizationMonoid.radical f} := by
  ext b
  simp only [Ideal.mem_radical_iff, Ideal.mem_span_singleton]
  exact exists_dvd_pow_iff_radical_dvd hf

/-- The radical of a nonzero principal ideal of a factorial domain is generated by a nonzero
element.  This is `UniqueFactorizationMonoid.radical_span_singleton` with the choice of a
normalization discharged, so that no normalization is named in the statement. -/
theorem exists_ne_zero_radical_span_singleton {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
    [UniqueFactorizationMonoid R] [IsDomain R] {f : R} (hf : f ≠ 0) :
    ∃ g : R, g ≠ 0 ∧ (Ideal.span {f}).radical = Ideal.span {g} := by
  let : StrongNormalizationMonoid R := UniqueFactorizationMonoid.strongNormalizationMonoid
  exact ⟨radical f, radical_ne_zero, radical_span_singleton hf⟩

end UniqueFactorizationMonoid

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The reduced induced closed subscheme on the complement of a dense affine open is an
effective Cartier divisor**, on a Noetherian scheme with affine diagonal whose local rings along
that complement are factorial.

This sharpens `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_compl_affineOpen`, which
produces an effective Cartier divisor supported on the complement but not the reduced one: the
divisor it builds is the product of the vanishing ideal sheaves of the irreducible components of
the complement.  The vanishing ideal sheaf of the complement is the radical of that product, and
the radical of an effective Cartier divisor is again an effective Cartier divisor when the local
rings are factorial, because the radical of a nonzero principal ideal of a factorial ring is
principal. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_vanishingIdeal_compl_denseAffineOpen
    (X : Scheme.{u}) [IsNoetherian X]
    [IsAffineHom (pullback.diagonal (terminal.from X))]
    (U : X.Opens) (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hdense : Dense (U : Set X))
    (hUFD : ∀ x : X, x ∉ U → UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk x)) :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsEffectiveCartierDivisor
      (Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal ⟨(U : Set X)ᶜ, U.2.isClosed_compl⟩) := by
  obtain ⟨I, hIcart, hIsupp⟩ :=
    exists_effectiveCartierDivisor_compl_affineOpen X U hU hdense hUFD
  have hsupp : I.support = (⟨(U : Set X)ᶜ, U.2.isClosed_compl⟩ : Closeds X) :=
    SetLike.coe_injective hIsupp
  rw [← hsupp, Scheme.IdealSheafData.vanishingIdeal_support]
  refine isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_stalk_regular_principal _ fun x hx => ?_
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.support_radical] at hx
  have hxU : x ∉ U := by
    have hmem : (x : X) ∈ (I.support : Set X) := hx
    rwa [hIsupp] at hmem
  have : UniqueFactorizationMonoid (X.presheaf.stalk x) := hUFD x hxU
  have : IsDomain (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    (isDomain_iff_cancelMulZero_and_nontrivial _).2 ⟨inferInstance, inferInstance⟩
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hxV, f, hf, hgen⟩ :=
    Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpen_ideal_eq_span_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor I hIcart x
  let : Algebra Γ(X, V) (X.presheaf.stalk x) := X.presheaf.algebra_section_stalk ⟨x, hxV⟩
  have : IsLocalization
      (hV.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxV⟩ : V)).asIdeal.primeCompl (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
    hV.isLocalization_stalk ⟨x, hxV⟩
  have hgerm : (X.presheaf.germ V x hxV).hom f ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ :=
      (IsLocalization.map_eq_zero_iff
        (hV.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxV⟩ : V)).asIdeal.primeCompl
        (S := X.presheaf.stalk x) f).1 h0
    have hm0 : (m : Γ(X, V)) = 0 := hf.right (by simpa using hm)
    exact m.2 (by rw [hm0]; exact Ideal.zero_mem _)
  obtain ⟨g, hg0, hgspan⟩ :=
    UniqueFactorizationMonoid.exists_ne_zero_radical_span_singleton hgerm
  refine ⟨g, isRegular_iff_ne_zero.mpr hg0, ?_⟩
  have hrad : IdealSheafData.stalk I.radical x = (IdealSheafData.stalk I x).radical := by
    rw [AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I.radical x ⟨V, hV⟩ hxV,
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ I x ⟨V, hV⟩ hxV,
      Scheme.IdealSheafData.radical_ideal]
    exact IsLocalization.map_radical
      (M := (hV.primeIdealOf (⟨x, hxV⟩ : V)).asIdeal.primeCompl)
      (S := X.presheaf.stalk x) (I.ideal ⟨V, hV⟩)
  rw [hrad, IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_span_germ_of_ideal_eq_span (U := ⟨V, hV⟩) hxV hgen, hgspan]

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
